for a decade Washington DC has been a  celebrated national model of school  reform then in January and audit showed  that one-third of DC's high school  graduates should not have received  diplomas indeed it turns out that the  system's true graduation rate is lower  than it was in 2011 how could this have  gone unnoticed blogger Alexander  Rousseau is placed part of the blame on  rank boosterism by the capital's  preeminent news outlet but this coverage  reflects a larger problem the bandwagon  mentality and school reform since 2007  philanthropists have poured more than a  hundred and twenty million dollars into  DC schools and advocates and think tanks  were lauded for glowing accounts of  developments in DC it was easy for  reformers to feel they'd be labeled  unhelpful or anti reform for going  off-script this all fueled or with us or  against us mindset then which no one  looked too hard for problems DC's should  be a wake-up call for a school reform  culture that has been heavy on  cheerleading and light on skepticism  what do you make of the Washington DC  graduation rate scandal let us know in  your comments also let us know what  other topics you'd like our scholars to  cover in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE  and subscribe for more research and  videos from AEI
 

